# =============================================================================
# frontend/.dockerignore
#
# Build-context hygiene for the Angular 19 workspace `dnn-migration`
# (AAP 0.2.1.2 CREATE target, placed at the workspace root by AAP 0.4.1.2,
# recorded as "no legacy equivalent" by AAP 0.5.1.6).
#
# ----------------------------- READ THIS FIRST -------------------------------
# THIS FILE DOES NOT GOVERN THE IMAGES THAT ARE ACTUALLY SHIPPED.
#
# The real Docker build context for BOTH images is the REPOSITORY ROOT, not
# this directory. The exclusion list Docker consults during validation Gate 6
# (`docker-compose build`) and Gate 7 (`docker-compose up -d`) is therefore
# the .dockerignore at the repository root - NOT this one. Three independent
# proofs:
#
#   1. docker/docker-compose.yml declares `context: ..` for both the `api`
#      and the `frontend` service. Relative to docker/, `..` is the
#      repository root.
#   2. docker/frontend.Dockerfile copies `frontend/package.json` and
#      `docker/nginx.conf`. Neither path is reachable from a context rooted
#      at frontend/, so the context cannot be this directory.
#   3. docs/project-guide.md L233-237 documents the per-image commands
#        docker build -f docker/api.Dockerfile      -t dnnmigration-api      .
#        docker build -f docker/frontend.Dockerfile -t dnnmigration-frontend .
#      The trailing `.` IS the context: the repository root.
#
# This file consequently governs ONLY a frontend-rooted context - a local
# experiment, a future per-application pipeline, or a tool invoked as
# `docker build ./frontend`. It deliberately does NOT compensate for anything
# the repository-root .dockerignore does: that file is what keeps the ~35 MB
# of read-only legacy VB.NET reference material out of the real context, and
# those trees are not inside frontend/, so they are correctly absent here.
#
# ------------------------------ DESIGN RULES ---------------------------------
# * Because this file is not load-bearing for the shipped images, an
#   accidental over-exclusion here fails SILENTLY and LATE. Only generated,
#   transient and machine-local material is excluded below. No source file
#   and no build configuration file is excluded, ever.
# * Nothing that `npm ci`, `ng build` or `ng test` needs may appear below.
#   That means package.json, the committed npm lockfile, angular.json, all
#   three tsconfig files, karma.conf.js, .nvmrc, the whole of src/ (every
#   component, every style partial, src/environments/* and every Jasmine
#   spec file) and the whole of public/ all stay in the context. Two of
#   those are hard gates: `npm ci` aborts outright without the committed
#   npm lockfile, and Gate 4 fails outright without karma.conf.js, which
#   supplies the ChromeHeadlessNoSandbox launcher that headless Chrome
#   needs in order to start as root.
# * This file contains no negation entry (no line beginning with an
#   exclamation mark) and no broad directory pattern, so no later line can
#   shadow an earlier one. Docker applies patterns in order and the last
#   match wins; the safest design is one that needs no ordering at all.
# * Version-control patterns are spelled out in full rather than globbed,
#   because public/.gitkeep is a required asset: it is what keeps the
#   angular.json assets glob (`input: "public"`) valid. A `.git*` wildcard
#   would silently empty public/ and break the production build.
#
# Pattern semantics: an unprefixed pattern is anchored at the context root; a
# `**/` prefix matches at any depth; a directory match excludes its subtree.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installed dependencies - the single most important entry.
# AAP 0.1.1.3: "A .dockerignore is required to keep node_modules, bin and obj
# out of the build contexts." docker/frontend.Dockerfile runs `npm ci` INSIDE
# the node:20-alpine build stage, so a host tree copied in would ship
# wrong-platform native bindings and defeat the deterministic, reproducible
# install that the committed npm lockfile exists to guarantee.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and compiler caches.
# `ng build --configuration production` emits dist/dnn-migration/browser
# inside the image; it is produced there and never copied in. out-tsc/ is the
# TypeScript outDir declared by tsconfig.app.json and tsconfig.spec.json.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/dist/
**/.angular/
out-tsc/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and coverage output.
# Gate 4 runs `ng test --watch=false --browsers=ChromeHeadless
# --code-coverage`, and karma.conf.js writes to coverage/dnn-migration, so
# these are real local artefacts on any developer machine.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/
karma-results*
chrome-profiler-events*.json
speed-measure-plugin*.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and package-manager caches.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.eslintcache
.npm/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version-control metadata. Enumerated exactly, and anchored at the context
# root, so that no pattern can reach public/.gitkeep (see DESIGN RULES above).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and operating-system noise.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/ehthumbs.db
**/Desktop.ini

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local environment overrides and credentials.
# NOTE: the workspace's real, committed configuration lives in
# src/environments/ (environment.ts and environment.development.ts, per
# AAP 0.4.1.2) and is NOT matched by anything here - every pattern in this
# group is anchored at the context root or keyed to a credential extension.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT excluded: .editorconfig, README.md and this file itself.
# Each is a few hundred bytes, sending them costs nothing measurable, and
# every additional entry here is one more chance to silently drop something
# a frontend-rooted build needs. Clarity is worth more than a minimal context.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
